      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Earth is the largest terrestrial planet and ranks fifth overall in size in the solar system.",
        "Planetary size determines gravitational strength, atmospheric retention, and liquid water viability.",
        "Strong gravity prevents Earth's atmosphere from escaping into space.",
        "Earth's moderate size avoids the crushing pressure characteristic of gas giants and allows stable temperatures."
      ],
